cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MissingPatterns.jl in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MissingPatterns.jl: terminal-based exploration of missing data patterns in Julia"
abstract: >-
  MissingPatterns.jl is a Julia package for exploring missing data patterns in
  any Tables.jl-compatible source. It renders missing-value heatmaps, unique
  missingness patterns, per-column and per-row summaries, pairwise
  co-occurrence of missingness and before/after diffs directly in the terminal
  using Unicode and ANSI truecolor, with no plotting-library dependencies. The
  same views are also available as Tables.jl row tables, and the heatmap can be
  exported as standalone HTML.
